## Keep make deploy from rebinding Lakebase off a sourced .env
================================================================================

Context: Redeploying ontobricks-09x while ``LAKEBASE_PROJECT`` was still
exported from ``.env`` overrode ``deploy.config.sh`` and rebound the app
postgres resource from ``ontobricks-demo-09-registry`` (the populated
registry) to ``ontobricks-dev-registry``. Domains were not deleted; the
app pointed at a different database.

Changes:

1. Makefile
   ``make deploy`` (and siblings) also unset ``LAKEBASE_*`` /
   ``APP_LAKEBASE_PROJECT`` / ``APP_LAKEBASE_BRANCH`` before
   ``scripts/deploy.sh``.
2. tests/units/settings/test_deploy_app_rename_guard.py
   Contract that the deploy recipes drop those env vars.

Modified files:
- Makefile
- tests/units/settings/test_deploy_app_rename_guard.py

Tests: uv run --frozen pytest -q -m "not scenario" → 9516 passed, 326 skipped, 8 deselected, 40 warnings in 54.06s

